{title: NEVER DID NO WANDERIN'}
{subtitle: The Folksmen}
     Using just the 1st string pick the string at the following frets:  0 - 0 - 3 - 5 - 7 - 5 - 3 - (2/3) - 0 - 0 - (2/3) - 0 - 0; (2/3) - 0 - 0 - 3 - 5 - 7 - 5 - 3 - (2/3) - 0 where (2/3) which means pick the 2nd string/3rd fret note (d).

     Using just the 2nd fret pick the notes using the 2nd, 3rd, and 4th strings:  <4c> <4c> <3o> <3c> <2o> <3c> <3o> <4o> <4c> <4c> <4o> <4c> <4c>; <4o> <4c> <4c> <3o> <3c> <2o> <3c> <3o> <4o> <4c> where the number is the string number and "c" means to cover the note (I use my index finger) and "o" means the string is open.  So "<4c>" is 4th string/2nd fret and "<3o>" is open third string, etc.   It's just sort of an on/off deal as you move down and up the strings.  Looks complicated but it's pretty easy once you do it once along with the recording.

Next the chord voicing.  It's one strum of (Em), then you lift off the (bottom) ring finger momentarily for one beat of the (Emsus2) and then two more strums of the (Em).  Also note this sequence repeats in the song but the thing is, that first (Em) in the sequence begins with the last word of the line.  Actually pretty easy.

